# Vercel does NOT honor .gitignore on CLI deploys — without this it uploads the
# whole ~3GB Unity repo (Library/, Temp/, Assets/, Builds/Windows, gitignored art
# packs) and fails the 2 GiB limit. Allowlist ONLY what the deployment serves:
#   - Builds/WebGL  → the static site root (vercel.json "outputDirectory")
#   - api/          → the serverless functions (incl. api/pi/verify.js)
#   - the configs   → vercel.json + package.json (+ lock) for the api deps
# This mirrors the gitignore intent (the heavy dirs are all gitignored too).

# 1) ignore every top-level entry
/*

# 2) re-include only what we serve
#    api/: full backend now ships — Vercel PRO lifts the Hobby 12-function cap (owner
#    upgraded 2026-07-01). All functions deploy (events/track, trace, save/load, pi/verify,
#    profile, referral, promo, leaderboard) so the client's telemetry + the WebTrace debug
#    sink reach Neon. DATABASE_URL must be set on the project.
!/api
!/vercel.json
!/package.json
!/package-lock.json
!/Builds

# 3) within Builds, keep ONLY the WebGL output (drop Builds/Windows etc.)
/Builds/*
!/Builds/WebGL
